===================== Grafana Dashboard =============

Connect Grafana to Prometheus
Open http://localhost:3000.

Step 1 — Sign in
        The default credentials for a fresh Grafana installation are generally:
        - Username: admin
        - Password: admin
        You may be prompted to change the password.

Step 2 — Add a data source
        Navigate to Connections → Data sources → Add data source → Prometheus.

Step 3 — Configure the URL
        Enter this URL:  http://prometheus:9090
    Click Save & test. Because Grafana and Prometheus are on the same Docker network, use the Compose service name prometheus, not localhost.

Create your first Grafana dashboard
        Go to Dashboards → New → New dashboard → Add visualization, select Prometheus as the data source, and enter one of these queries.


Application availability
    Visualization: Stat
    up{job="spring-boot"}
    A value of 1 means the target is up; 0 means it is down.


Request rate
    Visualization: Time series
    rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count[1m])
    Shows HTTP requests per second over time.


JVM heap memory
    Visualization: Time series
    sum(jvm_memory_used_bytes{area="heap"})
    Shows used heap memory in bytes.




